{"task_id": "Mbpp/223", "solution": "def _validate_inputs(array, n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Validates that n is equal to the length of the array.\n    Raises ValueError if n != len(array).\n    \"\"\"\n    if n != len(array):\n        raise ValueError(\"Input 'n' must be equal to the length of the array.\")\n\ndef _first_occurrence(array, n, element):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the first index of the element in a sorted array using binary search.\n    Returns -1 if the element is not found.\n    \"\"\"\n    low = 0\n    high = n - 1\n    result = -1\n    while low <= high:\n        mid = low + (high - low) // 2\n        if array[mid] == element:\n            result = mid\n            high = mid - 1  # Look for an earlier occurrence in the left half\n        elif array[mid] < element:\n            low = mid + 1\n        else:  # array[mid] > element\n            high = mid - 1\n    return result\n\ndef _last_occurrence(array, n, element):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the last index of the element in a sorted array using binary search.\n    Returns -1 if the element is not found.\n    \"\"\"\n    low = 0\n    high = n - 1\n    result = -1\n    while low <= high:\n        mid = low + (high - low) // 2\n        if array[mid] == element:\n            result = mid\n            low = mid + 1  # Look for a later occurrence in the right half\n        elif array[mid] < element:\n            low = mid + 1\n        else:  # array[mid] > element\n            high = mid - 1\n    return result\n\ndef is_majority(array, n, element):\n    \"\"\"\n    Determines if an element is the majority element in a sorted array.\n    The majority element occurs more than n/2 times.\n    \"\"\"\n    _validate_inputs(array, n)\n\n    first_idx = _first_occurrence(array, n, element)\n\n    if first_idx == -1:\n        return False  # Element not found in the array\n\n    last_idx = _last_occurrence(array, n, element)\n\n    # Calculate the count of occurrences\n    count = last_idx - first_idx + 1\n\n    # Check if the count is strictly greater than n/2\n    return count > (n / 2)"}
