{"task_id": "Mbpp/238", "solution": "def number_of_substrings(s: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts the number of non-empty substrings of a given string.\n    This includes substrings that are identical in content but differ by position.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(s, str):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input must be a string.\")\n\n    n = len(s)\n    # The number of non-empty substrings of a string of length n is given by the formula n * (n + 1) / 2.\n    # This formula inherently handles the empty string case (n=0) by returning 0.\n    return n * (n + 1) // 2"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/237", "solution": "from typing import List, Tuple, Dict\n\ndef check_occurences(tuples: List[Tuple[int,int]]) -> Dict[Tuple[int,int], int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Normalizes each 2-element tuple to (min, max) and aggregates counts.\n    Returns a dictionary mapping canonical tuples to their frequencies.\n    \"\"\"\n    counts: Dict[Tuple[int, int], int] = {}\n    for t in tuples:\n        # Normalize the tuple to its canonical (min, max) form\n        canonical = tuple(sorted(t))\n        counts[canonical] = counts.get(canonical, 0) + 1\n    return counts"}
